{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 00:52:13", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-94116da8-4a3a-4bd4-bc19-b2df54ede631', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "milestone": "Core Theming Infrastructure - Establish the foundation for the theming system with basic theme switching capabilities. Deliverables include theme data model and validation, theme API endpoints, theme persistence, and server-side theme validation.",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AHyZ1c3CY98kbmfyLCWsBm', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MaPjZcbWEATfb7MQHcTY4z', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AHyZ1c3CY98kbmfyLCWsBm', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Theming System - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Modular Frontend with Backend Support\\n- **Pattern**: Micro-frontend architecture with centralized theme management\\n- **Rationale**: Provides flexibility, scalability, and clear separation of concerns\\n- **Key Principle**: Decoupled theme system that can be easily integrated and extended\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React 18\\n- **Styling**: Styled-Components (CSS-in-JS)\\n- **State Management**: React Context API + Custom Theme Hook\\n- **Reasons**: \\n  - Excellent performance\\n  - Dynamic styling capabilities\\n  - Strong typing support\\n  - Easy theme variable management\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL for user theme storage\\n- **Reasons**:\\n  - Fast performance\\n  - Easy API development\\n  - Strong typing with Pydantic\\n  - Robust ORM capabilities\\n\\n### Additional Tools\\n- **State Persistence**: Local Storage + Server-side storage\\n- **Validation**: Joi/Zod for schema validation\\n- **Testing**: Jest (frontend), Pytest (backend)\\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. Theme Provider\\n- **Responsibility**: Global theme state management\\n- **Key Functions**:\\n  - Load initial theme\\n  - Broadcast theme changes\\n  - Validate theme data\\n  - Manage theme persistence\\n\\n### 2. Theme Editor\\n- **Responsibility**: User interface for theme customization\\n- **Key Features**:\\n  - Color picker\\n  - Typography controls\\n  - Live preview\\n  - Export/Import functionality\\n\\n### 3. Theme API Service\\n- **Responsibility**: Backend theme management\\n- **Endpoints**:\\n  - GET /themes (retrieve available themes)\\n  - POST /themes (save custom theme)\\n  - PUT /themes/:id (update theme)\\n  - DELETE /themes/:id (remove custom theme)\\n\\n### 4. Theme Validation Service\\n- **Responsibility**: Ensure theme data integrity\\n- **Checks**:\\n  - Color contrast ratios\\n  - CSS property validation\\n  - Accessibility compliance\\n\\n## D. File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nui-theming-system/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeProvider/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeEditor/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useTheme.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeService.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeValidation.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 app/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 models/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme_service.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 routes/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme_routes.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 validators/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme_validator.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 shared/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme-schema.json\\n```\\n\\n## E. Data Model\\n\\n### Theme Schema\\n```typescript\\ninterface Theme {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  colors: {\\n    primary: string;\\n    secondary: string;\\n    background: string;\\n    text: string;\\n  };\\n  typography: {\\n    fontFamily: string;\\n    fontSize: number;\\n    lineHeight: number;\\n  };\\n  spacing: {\\n    base: number;\\n    scale: number;\\n  };\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## F. API Design\\n\\n### Theme Endpoints\\n- `GET /themes` - List available themes\\n- `POST /themes` - Create custom theme\\n- `GET /themes/:id` - Retrieve specific theme\\n- `PUT /themes/:id` - Update theme\\n- `DELETE /themes/:id` - Delete theme\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Static hosting (Netlify/Vercel)\\n- CDN distribution\\n- Docker containerization\\n\\n### Backend\\n- Containerized deployment\\n- Kubernetes for scaling\\n- Database migrations with Alembic\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Unit Tests: Component rendering\\n- Integration Tests: Theme switching\\n- Accessibility Tests: Color contrast\\n- Performance Tests: Theme load time\\n\\n### Backend\\n- Unit Tests: Theme validation\\n- Integration Tests: API endpoints\\n- Security Tests: Input sanitization\\n\\n## I. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### CSS Modules vs Styled-Components\\n- **Styled-Components Chosen**\\n  - Pro: Dynamic styling\\n  - Pro: Easier theme management\\n  - Con: Slight performance overhead\\n\\n### Redux vs Context API\\n- **Context API Chosen**\\n  - Pro: Lightweight\\n  - Pro: Built-in React solution\\n  - Con: Less powerful for complex state\\n\\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n1. **Performance Overhead**\\n   - Mitigation: Lazy loading of themes\\n   - Mitigation: Minimal CSS variable usage\\n\\n2. **Browser Compatibility**\\n   - Mitigation: Polyfills for older browsers\\n   - Mitigation: Graceful degradation\\n\\n3. **Accessibility Challenges**\\n   - Mitigation: Automated contrast checking\\n   - Mitigation: WCAG 2.1 compliance tests\\n\\n## K. Open Questions\\n\\n1. How many pre-built themes should be included initially?\\n2. What is the acceptable performance budget for theme switching?\\n3. Should we support custom font uploads?\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a flexible, performant, and extensible UI theming system that meets all specified requirements while maintaining a clean, modular design."}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MaPjZcbWEATfb7MQHcTY4z', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Theming System - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nImplement a comprehensive UI theming system that allows users to customize the visual appearance of the application interface. This system should provide multiple pre-built themes and the ability to create custom themes.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n1. **Theme Management**: Provide a system to load, apply, and switch between different visual themes\\n2. **Pre-built Themes**: Include multiple professionally designed themes (light, dark, high contrast)\\n3. **Custom Theme Creation**: Allow users to create and save custom themes\\n4. **Real-time Preview**: Provide instant visual feedback when customizing themes\\n5. **Persistence**: Save user theme preferences and custom themes\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Theme Components\\n- **Color Schemes**: Primary, secondary, accent colors, backgrounds, text colors\\n- **Typography**: Font families, sizes, weights, line heights\\n- **Spacing**: Margins, padding, component spacing\\n- **Border Styles**: Border radius, border widths, shadow effects\\n- **Interactive States**: Hover, focus, active, disabled states\\n\\n### User Features\\n- **Theme Selector**: Dropdown or gallery view to browse and select themes\\n- **Theme Editor**: Visual interface to customize theme properties\\n- **Color Picker**: Advanced color selection with palette generation\\n- **Preview Mode**: Live preview of theme changes before applying\\n- **Export/Import**: Save themes as JSON files for sharing\\n- **Reset Functionality**: Restore default themes or revert changes\\n\\n### System Features\\n- **CSS Variable Integration**: Use CSS custom properties for dynamic theming\\n- **Component Integration**: Ensure all UI components support theming\\n- **Performance Optimization**: Efficient theme switching without page reload\\n- **Accessibility Compliance**: Maintain WCAG 2.1 AA contrast requirements\\n- **Responsive Design**: Themes work across all device sizes\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend (React)\\n- **Theme Provider**: React Context for theme state management\\n- **Theme Hook**: Custom hook for accessing current theme\\n- **CSS-in-JS Support**: Styled-components or similar for dynamic styling\\n- **Local Storage**: Persist theme preferences client-side\\n- **Theme Validation**: Ensure theme data integrity and accessibility\\n\\n### Backend (Python/FastAPI)\\n- **Theme API**: Endpoints for saving/loading custom themes\\n- **User Preferences**: Store theme preferences in user profiles\\n- **Theme Validation**: Server-side validation of theme data\\n- **Default Themes**: Serve pre-built theme configurations\\n\\n### Data Model\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"theme_id\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"description\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"colors\\": {\\n    \\"primary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"secondary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"background\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"surface\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"text_primary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"text_secondary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"error\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"warning\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"success\\": \\"#hex\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"typography\\": {\\n    \\"font_family\\": \\"string\\",\\n    \\"font_size_base\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"line_height\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"font_weights\\": {}\\n  },\\n  \\"spacing\\": {\\n    \\"base_unit\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"scale_factor\\": \\"number\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"borders\\": {\\n    \\"radius\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"width\\": \\"number\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Theme switching should occur within 200ms\\n- No visual flash or layout shift during theme changes\\n- Minimal impact on page load times\\n\\n### Accessibility\\n- Maintain minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio for normal text\\n- Maintain minimum 3:1 contrast ratio for large text\\n- Support high contrast mode for accessibility\\n- Keyboard navigation for theme selection\\n- Screen reader compatibility\\n\\n### Browser Support\\n- Modern browsers (Chrome 90+, Firefox 88+, Safari 14+, Edge 90+)\\n- CSS custom properties support required\\n- Local storage support required\\n\\n### Security\\n- Sanitize theme data to prevent XSS\\n- Validate color values and CSS properties\\n- Rate limiting on theme save operations\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **User Adoption**: Users can successfully switch between themes\\n2. **Customization**: Users can create and save custom themes\\n3. **Performance**: No performance degradation with theming enabled\\n4. **Accessibility**: All themes meet accessibility standards\\n5. **Integration**: Theming works across all application components\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- **Technology Stack**: Using React frontend with CSS-in-JS styling\\n- **Storage**: Local storage for client-side persistence, database for user accounts\\n- **Design System**: Existing component library that can be themed\\n- **User Authentication**: User accounts exist for saving custom themes\\n- **Browser Compatibility**: Targeting modern browsers with CSS custom property support\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- **Advanced Animations**: Complex transition effects during theme switching\\n- **Theme Marketplace**: Sharing themes between users (future feature)\\n- **Advanced Typography**: Custom font uploads or extensive typography controls\\n- **Print Themes**: Specialized themes for printing\\n- **Mobile App Theming**: Native mobile application theming\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- **Performance Budget**: Theme system should not increase page load time by more than 100ms\\n- **File Size**: Theme files should not exceed 50KB each\\n- **Browser Memory**: Minimize memory usage when multiple themes are loaded\\n- **Accessibility**: All themes must pass automated accessibility testing\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- **Component Library**: Existing UI components must support theme variables\\n- **Design System**: Design tokens and style guide for consistent theming\\n- **User System**: User authentication and preferences storage\\n- **API Infrastructure**: Backend endpoints for theme management\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. **Theme Management System**: Core theming infrastructure\\n2. **Pre-built Themes**: Light, dark, and high contrast themes\\n3. **Theme Editor Interface**: User interface for theme customization\\n4. **Documentation**: Developer and user documentation\\n5. **Test Suite**: Comprehensive testing including accessibility tests\\n6. **Migration Guide**: Instructions for applying themes to existing components"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0174e9r11LBdam6xWAbZ6nnr', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md', 'content': "# Backend Tasks - Milestone 1: Core Theming Infrastructure\n\n## Overview\nEstablish the foundation for the theming system with basic theme switching capabilities. This milestone focuses on the backend infrastructure needed to support theme persistence, validation, and API access.\n\n## Tech Stack (per Architecture)\n- **Framework**: FastAPI (Python)\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy ORM\n- **Validation**: Pydantic models\n- **Testing**: pytest with coverage\n\n---\n\n## Task Group 1: Database Foundation\n\n### Task 1.1: Database Connection Setup\n**Description**: Configure PostgreSQL database connection with SQLAlchemy async support and connection pooling.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] SQLAlchemy async engine configured\n- [ ] Connection pooling enabled with reasonable defaults (min=5, max=20)\n- [ ] Database URL configurable via environment variables\n- [ ] Health check endpoint for database connectivity\n- [ ] Connection error handling with retry logic\n\n**Dependencies**: None (foundational)\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/core/database.py`\n- `backend/app/core/config.py`\n\n---\n\n### Task 1.2: Theme Database Model\n**Description**: Create SQLAlchemy model for Theme entity with all required fields per the data model specification.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Theme model with fields: id (UUID), name, description, colors (JSONB), typography (JSONB), spacing (JSONB), borders (JSONB)\n- [ ] Timestamps: created_at, updated_at\n- [ ] is_system flag to distinguish pre-built themes from custom themes\n- [ ] user_id foreign key for custom themes (nullable for system themes)\n- [ ] Proper indexes on frequently queried fields (user_id, is_system, name)\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/models/theme.py`\n- `backend/app/models/__init__.py`\n\n---\n\n### Task 1.3: Database Migrations Setup\n**Description**: Configure Alembic for database migrations and create initial migration for Theme table.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Alembic configured with async SQLAlchemy support\n- [ ] Initial migration creates themes table\n- [ ] Migration includes all indexes\n- [ ] Rollback capability tested\n- [ ] Migration scripts work with empty database\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/alembic.ini`\n- `backend/alembic/env.py`\n- `backend/alembic/versions/001_create_themes_table.py`\n\n---\n\n## Task Group 2: Pydantic Schemas & Validation\n\n### Task 2.1: Theme Pydantic Schemas\n**Description**: Create Pydantic models for theme data validation, serialization, and API request/response handling.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] ColorScheme model with fields: primary, secondary, background, surface, text_primary, text_secondary, error, warning, success\n- [ ] Typography model with fields: font_family, font_size_base, line_height, font_weights\n- [ ] Spacing model with fields: base_unit, scale_factor\n- [ ] Borders model with fields: radius, width\n- [ ] ThemeCreate schema for POST requests\n- [ ] ThemeUpdate schema for PUT/PATCH requests (all fields optional)\n- [ ] ThemeResponse schema for API responses\n- [ ] ThemeList schema for paginated list responses\n\n**Dependencies**: None (can be developed in parallel with Task Group 1)\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/schemas/theme.py`\n- `backend/app/schemas/__init__.py`\n\n---\n\n### Task 2.2: Color Validation Service\n**Description**: Implement color validation including hex format validation and WCAG contrast ratio checking.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Validate hex color format (3 or 6 character hex with optional #)\n- [ ] Normalize colors to consistent format (#RRGGBB)\n- [ ] Calculate contrast ratio between two colors\n- [ ] Validate text/background combinations meet WCAG 2.1 AA (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text)\n- [ ] Return detailed validation errors with specific failing combinations\n- [ ] Support batch validation of entire color scheme\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/services/color_validator.py`\n\n---\n\n### Task 2.3: Theme Validation Service\n**Description**: Comprehensive theme validation service that validates all theme properties and ensures data integrity.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Validate all color values using color validation service\n- [ ] Validate typography values (font_size_base > 0, line_height > 0)\n- [ ] Validate spacing values (base_unit > 0, scale_factor > 0)\n- [ ] Validate borders values (radius >= 0, width >= 0)\n- [ ] Validate theme name (non-empty, max 100 chars, no XSS characters)\n- [ ] Return aggregated validation result with all errors\n- [ ] Provide accessibility score based on contrast ratios\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.2\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/services/theme_validator.py`\n\n---\n\n## Task Group 3: Theme Service Layer\n\n### Task 3.1: Theme Repository\n**Description**: Create data access layer for theme CRUD operations with proper async support.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] get_by_id(theme_id) - returns theme or None\n- [ ] get_all(user_id, include_system=True, skip, limit) - returns paginated themes\n- [ ] create(theme_data) - creates and returns new theme\n- [ ] update(theme_id, theme_data) - updates and returns theme\n- [ ] delete(theme_id) - soft delete or hard delete theme\n- [ ] exists(theme_id) - checks if theme exists\n- [ ] get_by_name(name, user_id) - find theme by name for uniqueness check\n- [ ] All methods use async/await pattern\n- [ ] Proper error handling for database errors\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2, Task 2.1\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/repositories/theme_repository.py`\n- `backend/app/repositories/__init__.py`\n\n---\n\n### Task 3.2: Theme Service\n**Description**: Business logic layer for theme operations including validation, authorization, and CRUD orchestration.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] create_theme(user_id, theme_data) - validates and creates theme\n- [ ] update_theme(user_id, theme_id, theme_data) - validates ownership and updates\n- [ ] delete_theme(user_id, theme_id) - validates ownership and deletes\n- [ ] get_theme(theme_id) - retrieves single theme\n- [ ] list_themes(user_id, include_system, pagination) - lists accessible themes\n- [ ] Enforce uniqueness of theme name per user\n- [ ] Prevent modification/deletion of system themes\n- [ ] Integrate validation service before create/update\n- [ ] Raise appropriate exceptions (NotFoundError, ForbiddenError, ValidationError)\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.1, Task 2.3\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/services/theme_service.py`\n- `backend/app/core/exceptions.py`\n\n---\n\n## Task Group 4: API Endpoints\n\n### Task 4.1: Theme API Router\n**Description**: Implement REST API endpoints for theme CRUD operations.\n\n**Endpoints**:\n- `GET /api/v1/themes` - List themes (paginated)\n- `POST /api/v1/themes` - Create custom theme\n- `GET /api/v1/themes/{theme_id}` - Get single theme\n- `PUT /api/v1/themes/{theme_id}` - Update theme\n- `DELETE /api/v1/themes/{theme_id}` - Delete theme\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] All endpoints implemented with proper HTTP methods\n- [ ] Request validation using Pydantic schemas\n- [ ] Response serialization using Pydantic schemas\n- [ ] Proper HTTP status codes (200, 201, 204, 400, 404, 403, 422)\n- [ ] Pagination support on list endpoint (page, page_size query params)\n- [ ] Filter support on list endpoint (include_system query param)\n- [ ] OpenAPI documentation with examples\n- [ ] Dependency injection for service layer\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.2\n\n**Complexity**: Medium\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/api/v1/themes.py`\n- `backend/app/api/v1/__init__.py`\n- `backend/app/api/__init__.py`\n\n---\n\n### Task 4.2: API Error Handling\n**Description**: Implement global exception handlers and error response formatting.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Global exception handler for application exceptions\n- [ ] Consistent error response format: {error: {code, message, details}}\n- [ ] Map domain exceptions to HTTP status codes\n- [ ] ValidationError -> 422 with field-level details\n- [ ] NotFoundError -> 404\n- [ ] ForbiddenError -> 403\n- [ ] Log errors appropriately (debug for client errors, error for server errors)\n- [ ] Hide internal error details in production\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 3.2 (needs exception types)\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/api/error_handlers.py`\n\n---\n\n### Task 4.3: FastAPI Application Setup\n**Description**: Configure FastAPI application with middleware, routers, and startup/shutdown events.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] FastAPI app instance with metadata (title, version, description)\n- [ ] CORS middleware configured (configurable origins)\n- [ ] Include theme router at /api/v1/themes\n- [ ] Database connection on startup\n- [ ] Database cleanup on shutdown\n- [ ] Health check endpoint at /health\n- [ ] OpenAPI schema available at /docs\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 4.1, Task 4.2, Task 1.1\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/main.py`\n\n---\n\n## Task Group 5: Default Themes Seeding\n\n### Task 5.1: Default Theme Definitions\n**Description**: Define the three pre-built system themes: Light, Dark, and High Contrast.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Light theme with professional light color scheme\n- [ ] Dark theme with professional dark color scheme  \n- [ ] High Contrast theme meeting WCAG AAA contrast requirements\n- [ ] All themes pass accessibility validation (4.5:1 contrast minimum)\n- [ ] Themes stored as Python constants or JSON files\n- [ ] Each theme has id, name, description, and all style properties\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 2.1\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/data/default_themes.py`\n\n---\n\n### Task 5.2: Database Seeder\n**Description**: Create database seeder to initialize default themes on first run.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- [ ] Seed default themes if they don't exist\n- [ ] Don't duplicate themes on subsequent runs (idempotent)\n- [ ] Can be run via CLI command or on app startup\n- [ ] Log seeding operations\n- [ ] Support --force flag to recreate default themes\n\n**Dependencies**: Task 5.1, Task 3.1\n\n**Complexity**: Simple\n\n**Files to Create**:\n- `backend/app/scripts/seed_themes.py`\n\n---\n\n## Task Dependency Graph\n\n```\nTask 1.1 (DB Connection)\n    └── Task 1.2 (Theme Model)\n            └── Task 1.3 (Migrations)\n            └── Task 3.1 (Repository)\n                    └── Task 3.2 (Service)\n                            └── Task 4.1 (API Router)\n                                    └── Task 4.3 (App Setup)\n\nTask 2.1 (Schemas) ─────────┬── Task 2.2 (Color Validation)\n                            │       └── Task 2.3 (Theme Validation)\n                            │               └── Task 3.2 (Service)\n                            └── Task 3.1 (Repository)\n                            └── Task 5.1 (Default Themes)\n                                    └── Task 5.2 (Seeder)\n\nTask 3.2 (Service) ─── Task 4.2 (Error Handling) ─── Task 4.3 (App Setup)\n```\n\n## Implementation Order (Critical Path)\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Parallel)\n1. **Task 1.1**: Database Connection Setup\n2. 