objectives and acceptance criteria defined\\n   - Scope constraints established\\n\\n2. \\u2705 **Architecture Design** - `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md`\\n   - State-Aware Data Refresh Pattern designed\\n   - Separation of concerns approach established\\n   - Custom hooks architecture (useViewState, useDataRefresh)\\n   - Component structure defined (TimelineContainer, MemoizedTimelineItems)\\n\\n3. \\u2705 **Task Breakdown** - `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md`\\n   - 6 detailed development tasks identified\\n   - Implementation order established\\n   - Time estimates provided (16-32 hours)\\n\\n4. \\u2705 **Test Strategy** - `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md`\\n   - Comprehensive test plan created\\n   - Performance benchmarks defined\\n   - Testing tools and frameworks selected\\n\\n### Current Analysis Findings:\\n\\n#### Existing Component Analysis:\\n- **Current File**: `HorizontalTimelineView.jsx` \\n- **Problem Root Cause**: Data refresh triggers useEffect \\u2192 fetchTimeline \\u2192 timelineData update \\u2192 full component re-render \\u2192 view reset\\n- **Key Issue**: No scroll position preservation during data updates\\n\\n#### Architecture Decisions Made:\\n- **Pattern**: State-Aware Data Refresh with controlled re-rendering\\n- **Tech Stack**: React hooks + Context API (existing React codebase)\\n- **Performance Strategy**: React.memo + useMemo for selective updates\\n- **Scroll Management**: Custom useViewState hook\\n\\n#### Implementation Plan Ready:\\n1. Custom hooks creation (useViewState, useDataRefresh)\\n2. Component wrapper development (TimelineContainer)  \\n3. Selective rendering optimization (MemoizedTimelineItems)\\n4. Performance monitoring integration\\n5. Cross-browser testing\\n\\n### Next Steps for Implementation:\\n1. **Create Custom Hooks** (2-4 hours)\\n   - useViewState for scroll position management\\n   - useDataRefresh for controlled data updates\\n   \\n2. **Develop Container Component** (4-6 hours)\\n   - TimelineContainer wrapper around existing HorizontalTimelineView\\n   - Integration of view state preservation\\n   \\n3. **Implement Memoized Components** (4-6 hours)\\n   - Selective re-rendering of timeline items\\n   - Performance optimization\\n\\n### Risk Assessment:\\n- **LOW RISK**: Well-defined problem with clear technical approach\\n- **MITIGATION**: Wrapper-based approach preserves existing functionality\\n- **FALLBACK**: Feature flag integration for quick rollback\\n\\n### Dependencies:\\n- All Milestone 1 dependencies satisfied\\n- Ready to proceed with implementation\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Ready for Milestone 2**: \\u2705 Core Fix Implementation"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Qj74tfKQdKxBapkMmv5LxK', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Qj74tfKQdKxBapkMmv5LxK', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Theming System - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nImplement a comprehensive UI theming system that allows users to customize the visual appearance of the application interface. This system should provide multiple pre-built themes and the ability to create custom themes.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n1. **Theme Management**: Provide a system to load, apply, and switch between different visual themes\\n2. **Pre-built Themes**: Include multiple professionally designed themes (light, dark, high contrast)\\n3. **Custom Theme Creation**: Allow users to create and save custom themes\\n4. **Real-time Preview**: Provide instant visual feedback when customizing themes\\n5. **Persistence**: Save user theme preferences and custom themes\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Theme Components\\n- **Color Schemes**: Primary, secondary, accent colors, backgrounds, text colors\\n- **Typography**: Font families, sizes, weights, line heights\\n- **Spacing**: Margins, padding, component spacing\\n- **Border Styles**: Border radius, border widths, shadow effects\\n- **Interactive States**: Hover, focus, active, disabled states\\n\\n### User Features\\n- **Theme Selector**: Dropdown or gallery view to browse and select themes\\n- **Theme Editor**: Visual interface to customize theme properties\\n- **Color Picker**: Advanced color selection with palette generation\\n- **Preview Mode**: Live preview of theme changes before applying\\n- **Export/Import**: Save themes as JSON files for sharing\\n- **Reset Functionality**: Restore default themes or revert changes\\n\\n### System Features\\n- **CSS Variable Integration**: Use CSS custom properties for dynamic theming\\n- **Component Integration**: Ensure all UI components support theming\\n- **Performance Optimization**: Efficient theme switching without page reload\\n- **Accessibility Compliance**: Maintain WCAG 2.1 AA contrast requirements\\n- **Responsive Design**: Themes work across all device sizes\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend (React)\\n- **Theme Provider**: React Context for theme state management\\n- **Theme Hook**: Custom hook for accessing current theme\\n- **CSS-in-JS Support**: Styled-components or similar for dynamic styling\\n- **Local Storage**: Persist theme preferences client-side\\n- **Theme Validation**: Ensure theme data integrity and accessibility\\n\\n### Backend (Python/FastAPI)\\n- **Theme API**: Endpoints for saving/loading custom themes\\n- **User Preferences**: Store theme preferences in user profiles\\n- **Theme Validation**: Server-side validation of theme data\\n- **Default Themes**: Serve pre-built theme configurations\\n\\n### Data Model\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"theme_id\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"description\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"colors\\": {\\n    \\"primary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"secondary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"background\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"surface\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"text_primary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"text_secondary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"error\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"warning\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"success\\": \\"#hex\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"typography\\": {\\n    \\"font_family\\": \\"string\\",\\n    \\"font_size_base\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"line_height\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"font_weights\\": {}\\n  },\\n  \\"spacing\\": {\\n    \\"base_unit\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"scale_factor\\": \\"number\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"borders\\": {\\n    \\"radius\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"width\\": \\"number\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Theme switching should occur within 200ms\\n- No visual flash or layout shift during theme changes\\n- Minimal impact on page load times\\n\\n### Accessibility\\n- Maintain minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio for normal text\\n- Maintain minimum 3:1 contrast ratio for large text\\n- Support high contrast mode for accessibility\\n- Keyboard navigation for theme selection\\n- Screen reader compatibility\\n\\n### Browser Support\\n- Modern browsers (Chrome 90+, Firefox 88+, Safari 14+, Edge 90+)\\n- CSS custom properties support required\\n- Local storage support required\\n\\n### Security\\n- Sanitize theme data to prevent XSS\\n- Validate color values and CSS properties\\n- Rate limiting on theme save operations\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **User Adoption**: Users can successfully switch between themes\\n2. **Customization**: Users can create and save custom themes\\n3. **Performance**: No performance degradation with theming enabled\\n4. **Accessibility**: All themes meet accessibility standards\\n5. **Integration**: Theming works across all application components\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- **Technology Stack**: Using React frontend with CSS-in-JS styling\\n- **Storage**: Local storage for client-side persistence, database for user accounts\\n- **Design System**: Existing component library that can be themed\\n- **User Authentication**: User accounts exist for saving custom themes\\n- **Browser Compatibility**: Targeting modern browsers with CSS custom property support\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- **Advanced Animations**: Complex transition effects during theme switching\\n- **Theme Marketplace**: Sharing themes between users (future feature)\\n- **Advanced Typography**: Custom font uploads or extensive typography controls\\n- **Print Themes**: Specialized themes for printing\\n- **Mobile App Theming**: Native mobile application theming\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- **Performance Budget**: Theme system should not increase page load time by more than 100ms\\n- **File Size**: Theme files should not exceed 50KB each\\n- **Browser Memory**: Minimize memory usage when multiple themes are loaded\\n- **Accessibility**: All themes must pass automated accessibility testing\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- **Component Library**: Existing UI components must support theme variables\\n- **Design System**: Design tokens and style guide for consistent theming\\n- **User System**: User authentication and preferences storage\\n- **API Infrastructure**: Backend endpoints for theme management\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. **Theme Management System**: Core theming infrastructure\\n2. **Pre-built Themes**: Light, dark, and high contrast themes\\n3. **Theme Editor Interface**: User interface for theme customization\\n4. **Documentation**: Developer and user documentation\\n5. **Test Suite**: Comprehensive testing including accessibility tests\\n6. **Migration Guide**: Instructions for applying themes to existing components"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0112uQjF8jrMq8XT4Cs3pFwN', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0112uQjF8jrMq8XT4Cs3pFwN', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Frontend Tasks: Timeline Scroll Preservation\\n\\n## Task 1: Create Scroll Position Management Hook\\n- **Description**: Implement `useViewState` custom hook for scroll position tracking\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Hook provides methods to preserve and restore scroll position\\n  * Supports both vertical and horizontal scroll tracking\\n  * Minimal performance overhead\\n- **Dependencies**: None\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours\\n\\n## Task 2: Implement Data Refresh Controller Hook\\n- **Description**: Create `useDataRefresh` hook to manage data refresh without view disruption\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Controls data refresh lifecycle\\n  * Prevents unnecessary re-renders\\n  * Provides refresh status and last update timestamp\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1 (Scroll Position Hook)\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 3-5 hours\\n\\n## Task 3: Create Memoized Timeline Items Component\\n- **Description**: Develop optimized timeline items component with selective rendering\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Uses React.memo for performance\\n  * Generates stable keys for items\\n  * Conditionally updates only when data changes\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Task 4: Update Timeline Container\\n- **Description**: Modify existing HorizontalTimelineView to integrate new scroll preservation logic\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Preserves user\'s scroll position during data refresh\\n  * No unexpected view shifts\\n  * Maintains existing functionality\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2, Task 3\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 5-7 hours\\n\\n## Task 5: Implement Performance Monitoring\\n- **Description**: Add analytics and performance tracking for scroll preservation\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Tracks view stability events\\n  * Monitors render time overhead\\n  * Collects anonymous usage data for improvement\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 4\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours\\n\\n## Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n- **Description**: Comprehensive testing across different browsers and devices\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Verified on Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\\n  * Consistent behavior on desktop and mobile\\n  * No performance regressions\\n- **Dependencies**: All previous tasks\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Total Estimated Effort\\n- **Development Time**: 16-32 hours\\n- **Calendar Time**: 1-2 weeks\\n- **Complexity**: High precision refactoring\\n\\n## Recommended Implementation Order\\n1. Task 1: Scroll Position Hook\\n2. Task 2: Data Refresh Controller\\n3. Task 3: Memoized Timeline Items\\n4. Task 4: Timeline Container Update\\n5. Task 5: Performance Monitoring\\n6. Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n\\n## Open Questions for Clarification\\n1. What is the acceptable performance overhead for scroll preservation?\\n2. Are there any specific browsers or devices of particular concern?\\n3. Should we implement a fallback mechanism for scroll restoration failures?"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 53.8%\n- Average iterations per task: 11.8\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Focus on completing tasks successfully - your success rate needs improvement.\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively managed the milestone completion by systematically tracking project progress, validating requirements, and ensuring all objectives were met with high-quality implementation and testing.\n- Successfully orchestrated complex model validation project by coordinating multiple agents, leveraging systematic approach to validate TDD Coordinator performance improvements. Project demonstrated ab...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a