{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 01:05:43", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-ea822a80-1d22-4e29-bd5c-516bb255c9ae', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Timeline Focus Preservation Fix"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014Kkn3FbbxYP7kDsy2j1rYw', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014Kkn3FbbxYP7kDsy2j1rYw', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Focus Preservation Fix - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nFix the HorizontalTimelineView component to preserve user scroll position and view focus during data refresh operations. The current implementation causes disruptive view resets that interrupt user workflow and degrade user experience.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n1. **View Stability**: Maintain user\'s scroll position during data refresh operations\\n2. **Performance Optimization**: Prevent unnecessary component re-renders during updates\\n3. **User Experience**: Eliminate view disruption and unexpected navigation jumps\\n4. **Backward Compatibility**: Preserve all existing HorizontalTimelineView functionality\\n5. **Code Quality**: Implement solution following TDD methodology and React best practices\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Core Fix Components\\n- **Scroll Position Management**: Track and preserve horizontal/vertical scroll positions\\n- **Selective Re-rendering**: Update only data that has changed, not view state\\n- **State Isolation**: Separate data refresh logic from view state management\\n- **Memory Management**: Efficient handling of view state without memory leaks\\n- **Performance Monitoring**: Track render performance and view stability metrics\\n\\n### User Experience Requirements\\n- **Seamless Updates**: Data refresh occurs without visible interruption to user\\n- **Position Preservation**: Exact scroll position maintained across refresh cycles\\n- **Smooth Performance**: No lag or stuttering during refresh operations\\n- **Visual Consistency**: No unexpected view shifts or layout jumps\\n- **Responsive Behavior**: Works consistently across different screen sizes\\n\\n### Technical Implementation\\n- **Custom Hooks**: useViewState and useDataRefresh for modular functionality\\n- **Component Wrapper**: TimelineContainer to integrate scroll preservation\\n- **Memoized Rendering**: Selective updates using React.memo and useMemo\\n- **Event Management**: Proper scroll event handling and cleanup\\n- **Cross-browser Support**: Consistent behavior across modern browsers\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend (React)\\n- **Custom Hook Architecture**: \\n  - `useViewState` for scroll position tracking and restoration\\n  - `useDataRefresh` for controlled data updates without view disruption\\n- **Component Structure**:\\n  - `TimelineContainer` wrapper around existing HorizontalTimelineView\\n  - `MemoizedTimelineItems` for selective rendering optimization\\n- **Performance Optimization**: React.memo, useMemo, and useCallback for efficient updates\\n- **State Management**: Minimal state changes to prevent unnecessary re-renders\\n\\n### Integration Requirements\\n- **Existing Component Preservation**: HorizontalTimelineView core functionality unchanged\\n- **API Compatibility**: Maintain current data fetching and refresh mechanisms\\n- **Event Handling**: Proper integration with existing scroll and interaction events\\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful fallback if scroll preservation fails\\n\\n### Implementation Tasks (from frontend_tasks_m1.md)\\n1. **Custom Hooks Creation** (2-4 hours)\\n   - useViewState for scroll position management\\n   - useDataRefresh for controlled data updates\\n\\n2. **Memoized Components** (4-6 hours)\\n   - React.memo optimization for timeline items\\n   - Stable key generation for efficient diffing\\n\\n3. **Container Integration** (5-7 hours)\\n   - TimelineContainer wrapper implementation\\n   - Integration of view state preservation logic\\n\\n4. **Performance Monitoring** (2-4 hours)\\n   - Analytics for view stability events\\n   - Render time tracking and optimization metrics\\n\\n5. **Cross-Browser Testing** (4-6 hours)\\n   - Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge compatibility\\n   - Mobile and desktop responsive behavior\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Scroll preservation overhead: < 5ms per refresh\\n- Memory usage: No significant increase during extended use\\n- Render performance: Maintain 60 FPS during scroll operations\\n- Data refresh speed: No impact on current refresh performance\\n\\n### Accessibility\\n- Keyboard navigation: Preserve focus state during refresh\\n- Screen reader compatibility: No accessibility regressions\\n- High contrast mode: Maintain visual consistency\\n- Reduced motion: Respect user motion preferences\\n\\n### Browser Support\\n- Modern browsers: Chrome 90+, Firefox 88+, Safari 14+, Edge 90+\\n- Scroll behavior: Consistent across different scrolling mechanisms\\n- Performance: Optimized for both desktop and mobile devices\\n\\n### Reliability\\n- Fallback mechanism: Graceful degradation if scroll preservation fails\\n- Error recovery: No application crashes due to view state issues\\n- Memory management: Proper cleanup of scroll event listeners\\n- Edge cases: Handle rapid refresh cycles and extreme scroll positions\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **User Focus Preservation**: Users maintain their viewing position during data refresh (100% success rate)\\n2. **Performance Metrics**: No measurable performance degradation in scroll or render operations\\n3. **Cross-Browser Compatibility**: Consistent behavior across all supported browsers\\n4. **Test Coverage**: 90% unit test coverage, 100% integration test coverage for view management\\n5. **User Experience**: No user-reported view disruption issues after implementation\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- **Performance Budget**: Maximum 5ms overhead per refresh operation\\n- **Memory Limit**: No more than 2MB additional memory usage\\n- **Bundle Size**: Implementation should not increase bundle size by more than 10KB\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Zero breaking changes to existing HorizontalTimelineView API\\n\\n## Implementation Strategy (TDD Approach)\\n1. **Test First**: Write comprehensive tests for scroll position management\\n2. **Red-Green-Refactor**: Implement minimal code to pass tests, then optimize\\n3. **Integration Testing**: Test complete user interaction flows\\n4. **Performance Testing**: Benchmark before and after implementation\\n5. **Cross-browser Validation**: Ensure consistent behavior across target browsers\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- **React**: Current version (18+) with hooks support\\n- **Existing Components**: HorizontalTimelineView component structure\\n- **Testing Framework**: Jest and React Testing Library setup\\n- **Development Environment**: Access to target browsers for testing\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- **Component Structure**: HorizontalTimelineView uses standard React patterns\\n- **Data Refresh Pattern**: Current data refresh triggers via useEffect/props changes\\n- **Scroll Implementation**: Standard browser scroll APIs are available\\n- **Performance Requirements**: Current performance is acceptable baseline\\n- **Browser Support**: Target modern browsers with CSS custom properties\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- **Complete Component Redesign**: Major architectural changes to timeline view\\n- **Advanced Animation**: Complex transition effects during updates\\n- **Mobile Native**: React Native or mobile app specific optimizations\\n- **Real-time Features**: WebSocket or real-time data streaming optimizations\\n- **Accessibility Overhaul**: Major accessibility improvements beyond maintaining current level\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n- **Feature Flags**: Implementation behind feature flag for safe rollback\\n- **Progressive Enhancement**: Core functionality works even if scroll preservation fails\\n- **Monitoring**: Performance and error tracking for production issues\\n- **Rollback Plan**: Quick revert process if issues arise in production\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. **Custom Hooks**: useViewState and useDataRefresh implementations\\n2. **Container Component**: TimelineContainer wrapper with scroll preservation\\n3. **Memoized Components**: Optimized timeline item rendering\\n4. **Test Suite**: Comprehensive unit and integration tests\\n5. **Performance Documentation**: Before/after performance analysis\\n6. **Implementation Guide**: Documentation for future maintenance and extension"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EMfANiXuEsg7S1kxTdcRuj', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Timeline Focus Preservation Fix - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nFix the HorizontalTimelineView component to preserve user scroll position and view focus during data refresh operations. This is a focused frontend optimization project requiring careful state management and performance optimization.\n\n## Milestone 1: Core Implementation and Testing (Primary Focus)\n**Objective**: Implement complete scroll preservation solution with full testing coverage\n**Duration**: 5-7 days\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. **Custom Hooks Implementation**\n   - `useViewState` hook for scroll position tracking/restoration\n   - `useDataRefresh` hook for controlled data updates\n   - Full unit test coverage for both hooks\n\n2. **Component Architecture**\n   - `TimelineContainer` wrapper component\n   - `MemoizedTimelineItems` optimized components\n   - Integration with existing HorizontalTimelineView\n   - Performance optimization using React.memo, useMemo, useCallback\n\n3. **Testing Suite**\n   - Unit tests for all custom hooks and components\n   - Integration tests for complete user interaction flows\n   - Cross-browser compatibility tests\n   - Performance benchmarking tests\n\n4. **Documentation**\n   - Implementation documentation\n   - Performance analysis (before/after)\n   - Integration guide for existing codebase\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- [ ] User scroll position preserved 100% during data refresh\n- [ ] No measurable performance degradation (<5ms overhead)\n- [ ] 90% unit test coverage, 100% integration test coverage\n- [ ] Works consistently in Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\n- [ ] No breaking changes to existing HorizontalTimelineView API\n- [ ] Memory usage remains stable (no leaks)\n\n### Implementation Tasks:\n1. Custom hooks creation and testing (frontend)\n2. Memoized component development (frontend)\n3. Container integration implementation (frontend)\n4. Performance monitoring setup (frontend)\n5. Cross-browser compatibility testing (frontend)\n\n## Milestone 2: Production Ready and Optimization (If Needed)\n**Objective**: Production deployment readiness and final optimizations\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\n\n### Deliverables:\n1. **Production Preparation**\n   - Feature flag implementation for safe rollback\n   - Error handling and graceful degradation\n   - Performance monitoring integration\n   - Production build optimization\n\n2. **Final Testing**\n   - End-to-end user acceptance testing\n   - Load testing with large datasets\n   - Mobile device testing\n   - Accessibility validation\n\n3. **Documentation Completion**\n   - User guide updates\n   - Maintenance documentation\n   - Rollback procedures\n   - Performance monitoring guide\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n- [ ] Feature flag controls enabled/disabled state\n- [ ] Graceful fallback if scroll preservation fails\n- [ ] Production monitoring shows stable performance\n- [ ] Mobile devices maintain same functionality\n- [ ] Accessibility features preserved\n- [ ] Complete rollback plan documented\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Frontend Implementation Strategy:\n1. **Custom Hook Architecture**: Modular, testable hooks for specific functionality\n2. **Component Wrapper Pattern**: Non-invasive integration with existing components\n3. **Performance Optimization**: Strategic use of React optimization patterns\n4. **Test-Driven Development**: Tests written before implementation\n5. **Cross-browser Testing**: Validated across target browser matrix\n\n### Risk Mitigation:\n- **Progressive Enhancement**: Core functionality preserved if optimization fails\n- **Feature Flags**: Safe rollback mechanism\n- **Monitoring**: Performance and error tracking\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Zero breaking changes to existing API\n\n### Success Metrics:\n- **View Stability**: 100% scroll position preservation\n- **Performance**: <5ms overhead per refresh operation\n- **Compatibility**: Consistent behavior across all supported browsers\n- **Test Coverage**: 90% unit, 100% integration test coverage\n- **User Experience**: Zero user-reported view disruption issues\n\n## Project Timeline\n- **Week 1**: Milestone 1 implementation and testing\n- **Week 2**: Milestone 2 production readiness (if needed)\n\n## Dependencies and Assumptions:\n- React 18+ with hooks support available\n- HorizontalTimelineView component uses standard React patterns\n- Current data refresh pattern is via useEffect/props changes\n- Standard browser scroll APIs available\n- Existing test infrastructure in place\n\nThis milestone plan focuses on delivering a high-quality, well-tested solution that preserves user experience while maintaining code quality and performance standards.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EMfANiXuEsg7S1kxTdcRuj', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260117_010540.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260117_010540.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KjioraCvmVZ5byDzSUTkXk', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Timeline Focus Preservation Fix'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KjioraCvmVZ5byDzSUTkXk', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Mile