{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 01:07:35", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1556e397-fba6-4718-81c6-bedf46a7d415', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "Timeline Focus Preservation Fix",\n  "description": "Fix HorizontalTimelineView to preserve user scroll position during data refresh"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AbqpTrx9MQFirYP6RAPq1z', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AbqpTrx9MQFirYP6RAPq1z', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Focus Preservation Fix - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nFix the HorizontalTimelineView component to preserve user scroll position and view focus during data refresh operations. The current implementation causes disruptive view resets that interrupt user workflow and degrade user experience.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n1. **View Stability**: Maintain user\'s scroll position during data refresh operations\\n2. **Performance Optimization**: Prevent unnecessary component re-renders during updates\\n3. **User Experience**: Eliminate view disruption and unexpected navigation jumps\\n4. **Backward Compatibility**: Preserve all existing HorizontalTimelineView functionality\\n5. **Code Quality**: Implement solution following TDD methodology and React best practices\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Core Fix Components\\n- **Scroll Position Management**: Track and preserve horizontal/vertical scroll positions\\n- **Selective Re-rendering**: Update only data that has changed, not view state\\n- **State Isolation**: Separate data refresh logic from view state management\\n- **Memory Management**: Efficient handling of view state without memory leaks\\n- **Performance Monitoring**: Track render performance and view stability metrics\\n\\n### User Experience Requirements\\n- **Seamless Updates**: Data refresh occurs without visible interruption to user\\n- **Position Preservation**: Exact scroll position maintained across refresh cycles\\n- **Smooth Performance**: No lag or stuttering during refresh operations\\n- **Visual Consistency**: No unexpected view shifts or layout jumps\\n- **Responsive Behavior**: Works consistently across different screen sizes\\n\\n### Technical Implementation\\n- **Custom Hooks**: useViewState and useDataRefresh for modular functionality\\n- **Component Wrapper**: TimelineContainer to integrate scroll preservation\\n- **Memoized Rendering**: Selective updates using React.memo and useMemo\\n- **Event Management**: Proper scroll event handling and cleanup\\n- **Cross-browser Support**: Consistent behavior across modern browsers\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend (React)\\n- **Custom Hook Architecture**: \\n  - `useViewState` for scroll position tracking and restoration\\n  - `useDataRefresh` for controlled data updates without view disruption\\n- **Component Structure**:\\n  - `TimelineContainer` wrapper around existing HorizontalTimelineView\\n  - `MemoizedTimelineItems` for selective rendering optimization\\n- **Performance Optimization**: React.memo, useMemo, and useCallback for efficient updates\\n- **State Management**: Minimal state changes to prevent unnecessary re-renders\\n\\n### Integration Requirements\\n- **Existing Component Preservation**: HorizontalTimelineView core functionality unchanged\\n- **API Compatibility**: Maintain current data fetching and refresh mechanisms\\n- **Event Handling**: Proper integration with existing scroll and interaction events\\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful fallback if scroll preservation fails\\n\\n### Implementation Tasks (from frontend_tasks_m1.md)\\n1. **Custom Hooks Creation** (2-4 hours)\\n   - useViewState for scroll position management\\n   - useDataRefresh for controlled data updates\\n\\n2. **Memoized Components** (4-6 hours)\\n   - React.memo optimization for timeline items\\n   - Stable key generation for efficient diffing\\n\\n3. **Container Integration** (5-7 hours)\\n   - TimelineContainer wrapper implementation\\n   - Integration of view state preservation logic\\n\\n4. **Performance Monitoring** (2-4 hours)\\n   - Analytics for view stability events\\n   - Render time tracking and optimization metrics\\n\\n5. **Cross-Browser Testing** (4-6 hours)\\n   - Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge compatibility\\n   - Mobile and desktop responsive behavior\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Scroll preservation overhead: < 5ms per refresh\\n- Memory usage: No significant increase during extended use\\n- Render performance: Maintain 60 FPS during scroll operations\\n- Data refresh speed: No impact on current refresh performance\\n\\n### Accessibility\\n- Keyboard navigation: Preserve focus state during refresh\\n- Screen reader compatibility: No accessibility regressions\\n- High contrast mode: Maintain visual consistency\\n- Reduced motion: Respect user motion preferences\\n\\n### Browser Support\\n- Modern browsers: Chrome 90+, Firefox 88+, Safari 14+, Edge 90+\\n- Scroll behavior: Consistent across different scrolling mechanisms\\n- Performance: Optimized for both desktop and mobile devices\\n\\n### Reliability\\n- Fallback mechanism: Graceful degradation if scroll preservation fails\\n- Error recovery: No application crashes due to view state issues\\n- Memory management: Proper cleanup of scroll event listeners\\n- Edge cases: Handle rapid refresh cycles and extreme scroll positions\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **User Focus Preservation**: Users maintain their viewing position during data refresh (100% success rate)\\n2. **Performance Metrics**: No measurable performance degradation in scroll or render operations\\n3. **Cross-Browser Compatibility**: Consistent behavior across all supported browsers\\n4. **Test Coverage**: 90% unit test coverage, 100% integration test coverage for view management\\n5. **User Experience**: No user-reported view disruption issues after implementation\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- **Performance Budget**: Maximum 5ms overhead per refresh operation\\n- **Memory Limit**: No more than 2MB additional memory usage\\n- **Bundle Size**: Implementation should not increase bundle size by more than 10KB\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Zero breaking changes to existing HorizontalTimelineView API\\n\\n## Implementation Strategy (TDD Approach)\\n1. **Test First**: Write comprehensive tests for scroll position management\\n2. **Red-Green-Refactor**: Implement minimal code to pass tests, then optimize\\n3. **Integration Testing**: Test complete user interaction flows\\n4. **Performance Testing**: Benchmark before and after implementation\\n5. **Cross-browser Validation**: Ensure consistent behavior across target browsers\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- **React**: Current version (18+) with hooks support\\n- **Existing Components**: HorizontalTimelineView component structure\\n- **Testing Framework**: Jest and React Testing Library setup\\n- **Development Environment**: Access to target browsers for testing\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- **Component Structure**: HorizontalTimelineView uses standard React patterns\\n- **Data Refresh Pattern**: Current data refresh triggers via useEffect/props changes\\n- **Scroll Implementation**: Standard browser scroll APIs are available\\n- **Performance Requirements**: Current performance is acceptable baseline\\n- **Browser Support**: Target modern browsers with CSS custom properties\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- **Complete Component Redesign**: Major architectural changes to timeline view\\n- **Advanced Animation**: Complex transition effects during updates\\n- **Mobile Native**: React Native or mobile app specific optimizations\\n- **Real-time Features**: WebSocket or real-time data streaming optimizations\\n- **Accessibility Overhaul**: Major accessibility improvements beyond maintaining current level\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n- **Feature Flags**: Implementation behind feature flag for safe rollback\\n- **Progressive Enhancement**: Core functionality works even if scroll preservation fails\\n- **Monitoring**: Performance and error tracking for production issues\\n- **Rollback Plan**: Quick revert process if issues arise in production\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. **Custom Hooks**: useViewState and useDataRefresh implementations\\n2. **Container Component**: TimelineContainer wrapper with scroll preservation\\n3. **Memoized Components**: Optimized timeline item rendering\\n4. **Test Suite**: Comprehensive unit and integration tests\\n5. **Performance Documentation**: Before/after performance analysis\\n6. **Implementation Guide**: Documentation for future maintenance and extension"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VJrQpyBJi4XApX7VCPRWtF', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': "# Timeline Focus Preservation Fix - Architecture Proposal\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n### Problem Statement\nPreserve user scroll position and view focus in the HorizontalTimelineView during data refresh operations without disrupting user experience.\n\n### Architectural Pattern\n**Approach**: Modular React Hooks Architecture with Memoized Rendering\n- Separate concerns between view state management and data refresh\n- Leverage React's performance optimization techniques\n- Implement lightweight, composable solution\n\n## 2. Tech Stack\n\n### Frontend Technologies\n- **Framework**: React 18+ \n- **State Management**: React Hooks (useState, useCallback, useMemo)\n- **Performance Optimization**: React.memo\n- **Testing**: \n  - Jest\n  - React Testing Library\n  - Performance profiling tools\n\n### Rationale\n- React Hooks provide flexible, lightweight state management\n- Minimal additional dependencies reduce complexity\n- Native React performance optimization techniques\n- Maintains existing component architecture\n\n## 3. System Components\n\n### Key Components\n1. **useViewState Hook**\n   - Manages scroll position tracking\n   - Stores and restores scroll state\n   - Handles different scroll types (horizontal/vertical)\n\n2. **useDataRefresh Hook**\n   - Manages data update logic\n   - Prevents unnecessary re-renders\n   - Controls refresh cycle\n\n3. **TimelineContainer**\n   - Wraps existing HorizontalTimelineView\n   - Integrates scroll preservation logic\n   - Manages component lifecycle\n\n4. **MemoizedTimelineItems**\n   - Optimized rendering of timeline items\n   - Uses stable keys for efficient updates\n   - Prevents unnecessary re-renders\n\n## 4. Data Flow Diagram\n\n```\n[Data Source] \n    ↓\n[useDataRefresh Hook]\n    ↓\n[MemoizedTimelineItems]\n    ↓\n[TimelineContainer] \n    ↓\n[useViewState Hook] \n    ↓\n[HorizontalTimelineView]\n```\n\n## 5. Implementation Details\n\n### Scroll Preservation Strategy\n```typescript\nfunction useViewState() {\n  const [scrollPosition, setScrollPosition] = useState({x: 0, y: 0});\n  \n  const captureScrollPosition = useCallback((element) => {\n    setScrollPosition({\n      x: element.scrollLeft,\n      y: element.scrollTop\n    });\n  }, []);\n\n  const restoreScrollPosition = useCallback((element) => {\n    if (element) {\n      element.scrollLeft = scrollPosition.x;\n      element.scrollTop = scrollPosition.y;\n    }\n  }, [scrollPosition]);\n\n  return { captureScrollPosition, restoreScrollPosition };\n}\n```\n\n### Data Refresh Hook\n```typescript\nfunction useDataRefresh(data, refreshFunction) {\n  const [currentData, setCurrentData] = useState(data);\n  \n  const refreshData = useCallback(async () => {\n    const newData = await refreshFunction();\n    setCurrentData(prevData => {\n      // Efficient update only for changed items\n      return newData.map(newItem => \n        prevData.find(item => item.id === newItem.id) || newItem\n      );\n    });\n  }, [refreshFunction]);\n\n  return { currentData, refreshData };\n}\n```\n\n## 6. Performance Considerations\n- Memoization to prevent unnecessary re-renders\n- Minimal state updates\n- Efficient scroll position tracking\n- Low overhead (<5ms per refresh)\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n- Unit tests for hooks\n- Integration tests for scroll preservation\n- Performance benchmarking\n- Cross-browser compatibility testing\n\n## 8. Risks and Mitigations\n- **Risk**: Performance overhead\n  - **Mitigation**: Strict performance budgeting, profiling\n- **Risk**: Browser compatibility\n  - **Mitigation**: Comprehensive cross-browser testing\n- **Risk**: Unexpected behavior\n  - **Mitigation**: Fallback mechanisms, feature flags\n\n## 9. Deployment Considerations\n- Feature flag for safe rollout\n- Gradual implementation\n- Performance monitoring in production\n\n## 10. Open Questions\n- Validate exact performance impact\n- Confirm behavior in edge cases (rapid refreshes)\n- Verify minimal bundle size increase\n\n## Conclusion\nA lightweight, efficient solution leveraging React's native performance optimization techniques to preserve user focus during timeline updates."}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VJrQpyBJi4XApX7VCPRWtF', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260117_010735.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260117_010735.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 94.6%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.4\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- Successfully analyzed the focus disruption requirements and designed a targeted architectural solution that balances user experience with performance constraints. The proposal provides concrete implem...\n- Successfully translated the focus disruption problem into a clear architectural solution emphasizing separation of concerns. The proposal provides concrete implementation details with React hooks whil...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
