objectives and acceptance criteria defined\\n   - Scope constraints established\\n\\n2. \\u2705 **Architecture Design** - `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md`\\n   - State-Aware Data Refresh Pattern designed\\n   - Separation of concerns approach established\\n   - Custom hooks architecture (useViewState, useDataRefresh)\\n   - Component structure defined (TimelineContainer, MemoizedTimelineItems)\\n\\n3. \\u2705 **Task Breakdown** - `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md`\\n   - 6 detailed development tasks identified\\n   - Implementation order established\\n   - Time estimates provided (16-32 hours)\\n\\n4. \\u2705 **Test Strategy** - `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md`\\n   - Comprehensive test plan created\\n   - Performance benchmarks defined\\n   - Testing tools and frameworks selected\\n\\n### Current Analysis Findings:\\n\\n#### Existing Component Analysis:\\n- **Current File**: `HorizontalTimelineView.jsx` \\n- **Problem Root Cause**: Data refresh triggers useEffect \\u2192 fetchTimeline \\u2192 timelineData update \\u2192 full component re-render \\u2192 view reset\\n- **Key Issue**: No scroll position preservation during data updates\\n\\n#### Architecture Decisions Made:\\n- **Pattern**: State-Aware Data Refresh with controlled re-rendering\\n- **Tech Stack**: React hooks + Context API (existing React codebase)\\n- **Performance Strategy**: React.memo + useMemo for selective updates\\n- **Scroll Management**: Custom useViewState hook\\n\\n#### Implementation Plan Ready:\\n1. Custom hooks creation (useViewState, useDataRefresh)\\n2. Component wrapper development (TimelineContainer)  \\n3. Selective rendering optimization (MemoizedTimelineItems)\\n4. Performance monitoring integration\\n5. Cross-browser testing\\n\\n### Next Steps for Implementation:\\n1. **Create Custom Hooks** (2-4 hours)\\n   - useViewState for scroll position management\\n   - useDataRefresh for controlled data updates\\n   \\n2. **Develop Container Component** (4-6 hours)\\n   - TimelineContainer wrapper around existing HorizontalTimelineView\\n   - Integration of view state preservation\\n   \\n3. **Implement Memoized Components** (4-6 hours)\\n   - Selective re-rendering of timeline items\\n   - Performance optimization\\n\\n### Risk Assessment:\\n- **LOW RISK**: Well-defined problem with clear technical approach\\n- **MITIGATION**: Wrapper-based approach preserves existing functionality\\n- **FALLBACK**: Feature flag integration for quick rollback\\n\\n### Dependencies:\\n- All Milestone 1 dependencies satisfied\\n- Ready to proceed with implementation\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Ready for Milestone 2**: \\u2705 Core Fix Implementation"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Qj74tfKQdKxBapkMmv5LxK', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Qj74tfKQdKxBapkMmv5LxK', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Theming System - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nImplement a comprehensive UI theming system that allows users to customize the visual appearance of the application interface. This system should provide multiple pre-built themes and the ability to create custom themes.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n1. **Theme Management**: Provide a system to load, apply, and switch between different visual themes\\n2. **Pre-built Themes**: Include multiple professionally designed themes (light, dark, high contrast)\\n3. **Custom Theme Creation**: Allow users to create and save custom themes\\n4. **Real-time Preview**: Provide instant visual feedback when customizing themes\\n5. **Persistence**: Save user theme preferences and custom themes\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Theme Components\\n- **Color Schemes**: Primary, secondary, accent colors, backgrounds, text colors\\n- **Typography**: Font families, sizes, weights, line heights\\n- **Spacing**: Margins, padding, component spacing\\n- **Border Styles**: Border radius, border widths, shadow effects\\n- **Interactive States**: Hover, focus, active, disabled states\\n\\n### User Features\\n- **Theme Selector**: Dropdown or gallery view to browse and select themes\\n- **Theme Editor**: Visual interface to customize theme properties\\n- **Color Picker**: Advanced color selection with palette generation\\n- **Preview Mode**: Live preview of theme changes before applying\\n- **Export/Import**: Save themes as JSON files for sharing\\n- **Reset Functionality**: Restore default themes or revert changes\\n\\n### System Features\\n- **CSS Variable Integration**: Use CSS custom properties for dynamic theming\\n- **Component Integration**: Ensure all UI components support theming\\n- **Performance Optimization**: Efficient theme switching without page reload\\n- **Accessibility Compliance**: Maintain WCAG 2.1 AA contrast requirements\\n- **Responsive Design**: Themes work across all device sizes\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend (React)\\n- **Theme Provider**: React Context for theme state management\\n- **Theme Hook**: Custom hook for accessing current theme\\n- **CSS-in-JS Support**: Styled-components or similar for dynamic styling\\n- **Local Storage**: Persist theme preferences client-side\\n- **Theme Validation**: Ensure theme data integrity and accessibility\\n\\n### Backend (Python/FastAPI)\\n- **Theme API**: Endpoints for saving/loading custom themes\\n- **User Preferences**: Store theme preferences in user profiles\\n- **Theme Validation**: Server-side validation of theme data\\n- **Default Themes**: Serve pre-built theme configurations\\n\\n### Data Model\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"theme_id\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"description\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"colors\\": {\\n    \\"primary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"secondary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"background\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"surface\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"text_primary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"text_secondary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"error\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"warning\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"success\\": \\"#hex\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"typography\\": {\\n    \\"font_family\\": \\"string\\",\\n    \\"font_size_base\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"line_height\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"font_weights\\": {}\\n  },\\n  \\"spacing\\": {\\n    \\"base_unit\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"scale_factor\\": \\"number\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"borders\\": {\\n    \\"radius\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"width\\": \\"number\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Theme switching should occur within 200ms\\n- No visual flash or layout shift during theme changes\\n- Minimal impact on page load times\\n\\n### Accessibility\\n- Maintain minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio for normal text\\n- Maintain minimum 3:1 contrast ratio for large text\\n- Support high contrast mode for accessibility\\n- Keyboard navigation for theme selection\\n- Screen reader compatibility\\n\\n### Browser Support\\n- Modern browsers (Chrome 90+, Firefox 88+, Safari 14+, Edge 90+)\\n- CSS custom properties support required\\n- Local storage support required\\n\\n### Security\\n- Sanitize theme data to prevent XSS\\n- Validate color values and CSS properties\\n- Rate limiting on theme save operations\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **User Adoption**: Users can successfully switch between themes\\n2. **Customization**: Users can create and save custom themes\\n3. **Performance**: No performance degradation with theming enabled\\n4. **Accessibility**: All themes meet accessibility standards\\n5. **Integration**: Theming works across all application components\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- **Technology Stack**: Using React frontend with CSS-in-JS styling\\n- **Storage**: Local storage for client-side persistence, database for user accounts\\n- **Design System**: Existing component library that can be themed\\n- **User Authentication**: User accounts exist for saving custom themes\\n- **Browser Compatibility**: Targeting modern browsers with CSS custom property support\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- **Advanced Animations**: Complex transition effects during theme switching\\n- **Theme Marketplace**: Sharing themes between users (future feature)\\n- **Advanced Typography**: Custom font uploads or extensive typography controls\\n- **Print Themes**: Specialized themes for printing\\n- **Mobile App Theming**: Native mobile application theming\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- **Performance Budget**: Theme system should not increase page load time by more than 100ms\\n- **File Size**: Theme files should not exceed 50KB each\\n- **Browser Memory**: Minimize memory usage when multiple themes are loaded\\n- **Accessibility**: All themes must pass automated accessibility testing\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- **Component Library**: Existing UI components must support theme variables\\n- **Design System**: Design tokens and style guide for consistent theming\\n- **User System**: User authentication and preferences storage\\n- **API Infrastructure**: Backend endpoints for theme management\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. **Theme Management System**: Core theming infrastructure\\n2. **Pre-built Themes**: Light, dark, and high contrast themes\\n3. **Theme Editor Interface**: User interface for theme customization\\n4. **Documentation**: Developer and user documentation\\n5. **Test Suite**: Comprehensive testing including accessibility tests\\n6. **Migration Guide**: Instructions for applying themes to existing components"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0112uQjF8jrMq8XT4Cs3pFwN', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0112uQjF8jrMq8XT4Cs3pFwN', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Frontend Tasks: Timeline Scroll Preservation\\n\\n## Task 1: Create Scroll Position Management Hook\\n- **Description**: Implement `useViewState` custom hook for scroll position tracking\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Hook provides methods to preserve and restore scroll position\\n  * Supports both vertical and horizontal scroll tracking\\n  * Minimal performance overhead\\n- **Dependencies**: None\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours\\n\\n## Task 2: Implement Data Refresh Controller Hook\\n- **Description**: Create `useDataRefresh` hook to manage data refresh without view disruption\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Controls data refresh lifecycle\\n  * Prevents unnecessary re-renders\\n  * Provides refresh status and last update timestamp\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1 (Scroll Position Hook)\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 3-5 hours\\n\\n## Task 3: Create Memoized Timeline Items Component\\n- **Description**: Develop optimized timeline items component with selective rendering\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Uses React.memo for performance\\n  * Generates stable keys for items\\n  * Conditionally updates only when data changes\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Task 4: Update Timeline Container\\n- **Description**: Modify existing HorizontalTimelineView to integrate new scroll preservation logic\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Preserves user\'s scroll position during data refresh\\n  * No unexpected view shifts\\n  * Maintains existing functionality\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2, Task 3\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 5-7 hours\\n\\n## Task 5: Implement Performance Monitoring\\n- **Description**: Add analytics and performance tracking for scroll preservation\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Tracks view stability events\\n  * Monitors render time overhead\\n  * Collects anonymous usage data for improvement\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 4\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours\\n\\n## Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n- **Description**: Comprehensive testing across different browsers and devices\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Verified on Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\\n  * Consistent behavior on desktop and mobile\\n  * No performance regressions\\n- **Dependencies**: All previous tasks\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Total Estimated Effort\\n- **Development Time**: 16-32 hours\\n- **Calendar Time**: 1-2 weeks\\n- **Complexity**: High precision refactoring\\n\\n## Recommended Implementation Order\\n1. Task 1: Scroll Position Hook\\n2. Task 2: Data Refresh Controller\\n3. Task 3: Memoized Timeline Items\\n4. Task 4: Timeline Container Update\\n5. Task 5: Performance Monitoring\\n6. Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n\\n## Open Questions for Clarification\\n1. What is the acceptable performance overhead for scroll preservation?\\n2. Are there any specific browsers or devices of particular concern?\\n3. Should we implement a fallback mechanism for scroll restoration failures?"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01GCG4wNQGubSMDtmsrydQXi', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GCG4wNQGubSMDtmsrydQXi', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Test Strategy: Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix\\n\\n## Objective\\nEnsure scroll preservation in HorizontalTimelineView during data refresh, preventing user focus disruption.\\n\\n## Test Coverage Strategy\\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 90% for custom hooks and utility functions\\n- **Integration Test Coverage**: 100% for view state management\\n- **End-to-End Test Coverage**: Critical user interaction flows\\n\\n## Test Task Breakdown\\n\\n### 1. useViewState Hook Tests\\n- [ ] Verify scroll position tracking\\n- [ ] Test position preservation mechanism\\n- [ ] Validate scroll restoration functionality\\n- [ ] Check memory management and cleanup\\n\\n### 2. useDataRefresh Hook Tests\\n- [ ] Validate data refresh without view disruption\\n- [ ] Test refresh state management\\n- [ ] Verify performance during rapid successive refreshes\\n- [ ] Ensure no unexpected re-renders\\n\\n### 3. TimelineContainer Component Tests\\n- [ ] Confirm view state isolation\\n- [ ] Test integration of view state and data refresh\\n- [ ] Validate memoization effectiveness\\n- [ ] Check cross-browser scroll behavior\\n\\n### 4. Performance and Edge Case Tests\\n- [ ] Measure render time overhead\\n- [ ] Test with large datasets\\n- [ ] Validate behavior under slow network conditions\\n- [ ] Check memory usage during extended use\\n\\n### 5. End-to-End Interaction Tests\\n- [ ] Simulate real-world user scrolling during data refresh\\n- [ ] Test multiple rapid data updates\\n- [ ] Verify no unexpected view shifts\\n- [ ] Validate smooth user experience\\n\\n## Testing Tools and Frameworks\\n- **Unit Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library\\n- **Performance Testing**: React DevTools Profiler\\n- **E2E Testing**: Playwright\\n- **Scroll Simulation**: Custom scroll event generators\\n\\n## Specific Test Scenarios\\n\\n### Positive Scenarios\\n1. User scrolls midway through timeline\\n2. Data refresh occurs without changing scroll position\\n3. Multiple rapid data updates\\n4. Large dataset with continuous updates\\n\\n### Negative/Edge Scenarios\\n1. Extremely fast scroll during refresh\\n2. Refresh during scroll momentum\\n3. Low-performance devices\\n4. Interrupted network conditions\\n\\n## Performance Benchmarks\\n- **Render Time**: &lt; 5ms overhead\\n- **Memory Usage**: No significant increase\\n- **Scroll Smoothness**: 60 FPS minimum\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation Tests\\n- Verify fallback mechanisms\\n- Test feature flag integration\\n- Validate graceful degradation\\n\\n## Recommended Test Sequence\\n1. Unit tests for individual hooks\\n2. Component integration tests\\n3. Performance benchmark tests\\n4. End-to-end user flow tests\\n5. Cross-browser compatibility tests\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign testing\\n- Testing unrelated components\\n- Network layer testing beyond current implementation\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Comprehensive test coverage report\\n- Performance metrics documentation\\n- Recommendations for further optimization"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011wd5eoDjXCJGuTge2SXyng', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011wd5eoDjXCJGuTge2SXyng', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Theming System - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Modular Frontend with Backend Support\\n- **Pattern**: Micro-frontend architecture with centralized theme management\\n- **Rationale**: Provides flexibility, scalability, and clear separation of concerns\\n- **Key Principle**: Decoupled theme system that can be easily integrated and extended\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React 18\\n- **Styling**: Styled-Components (CSS-in-JS)\\n- **State Management**: React Context API + Custom Theme Hook\\n- **Reasons**: \\n  - Excellent performance\\n  - Dynamic styling capabilities\\n  - Strong typing support\\n  - Easy theme variable management\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL for user theme storage\\n- **Reasons**:\\n  - Fast performance\\n  - Easy API development\\n  - Strong typing with Pydantic\\n  - Robust ORM capabilities\\n\\n### Additional Tools\\n- **State Persistence**: Local Storage + Server-side storage\\n- **Validation**: Joi/Zod for schema validation\\n- **Testing**: Jest (frontend), Pytest (backend)\\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. Theme Provider\\n- **Responsibility**: Global theme state management\\n- **Key Functions**:\\n  - Load initial theme\\n  - Broadcast theme changes\\n  - Validate theme data\\n  - Manage theme persistence\\n\\n### 2. Theme Editor\\n- **Responsibility**: User interface for theme customization\\n- **Key Features**:\\n  - Color picker\\n  - Typography controls\\n  - Live preview\\n  - Export/Import functionality\\n\\n### 3. Theme API Service\\n- **Responsibility**: Backend theme management\\n- **Endpoints**:\\n  - GET /themes (retrieve available themes)\\n  - POST /themes (save custom theme)\\n  - PUT /themes/:id (update theme)\\n  - DELETE /themes/:id (remove custom theme)\\n\\n### 4. Theme Validation Service\\n- **Responsibility**: Ensure theme data integrity\\n- **Checks**:\\n  - Color contrast ratios\\n  - CSS property validation\\n  - Accessibility compliance\\n\\n## D. File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nui-theming-system/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeProvider/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeEditor/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useTheme.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeService.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeValidation.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 app/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 models/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme_service.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 routes/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme_routes.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 validators/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme_validator.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 shared/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme-schema.json\\n```\\n\\n## E. Data Model\\n\\n### Theme Schema\\n```typescript\\ninterface Theme {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  colors: {\\n    primary: string;\\n    secondary: string;\\n    background: string;\\n    text: string;\\n  };\\n  typography: {\\n    fontFamily: string;\\n    fontSize: number;\\n    lineHeight: number;\\n  };\\n  spacing: {\\n    base: number;\\n    scale: number;\\n  };\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## F. API Design\\n\\n### Theme Endpoints\\n- `GET /themes` - List available themes\\n- `POST /themes` - Create custom theme\\n- `GET /themes/:id` - Retrieve specific theme\\n- `PUT /themes/:id` - Update theme\\n- `DELETE /themes/:id` - Delete theme\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Static hosting (Netlify/Vercel)\\n- CDN distribution\\n- Docker containerization\\n\\n### Backend\\n- Containerized deployment\\n- Kubernetes for scaling\\n- Database migrations with Alembic\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Unit Tests: Component rendering\\n- Integration Tests: Theme switching\\n- Accessibility Tests: Color contrast\\n- Performance Tests: Theme load time\\n\\n### Backend\\n- Unit Tests: Theme validation\\n- Integration Tests: API endpoints\\n- Security Tests: Input sanitization\\n\\n## I. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### CSS Modules vs Styled-Components\\n- **Styled-Components Chosen**\\n  - Pro: Dynamic styling\\n  - Pro: Easier theme management\\n  - Con: Slight performance overhead\\n\\n### Redux vs Context API\\n- **Context API Chosen**\\n  - Pro: Lightweight\\n  - Pro: Built-in React solution\\n  - Con: Less powerful for complex state\\n\\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n1. **Performance Overhead**\\n   - Mitigation: Lazy loading of themes\\n   - Mitigation: Minimal CSS variable usage\\n\\n2. **Browser Compatibility**\\n   - Mitigation: Polyfills for older browsers\\n   - Mitigation: Graceful degradation\\n\\n3. **Accessibility Challenges**\\n   - Mitigation: Automated contrast checking\\n   - Mitigation: WCAG 2.1 compliance tests\\n\\n## K. Open Questions\\n\\n1. How many pre-built themes should be included initially?\\n2. What is the acceptable performance budget for theme switching?\\n3. Should we support custom font uploads?\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a flexible, performant, and extensible UI theming system that meets all specified requirements while maintaining a clean, modular design."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FhzC1nSK1i7Pis1wjPNoYq', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Timeline Focus Preservation Fix', 'description': 'Implement timeline scroll preservation during data refresh to prevent user focus disruption in HorizontalTimelineView component. Milestone 1 analysis complete, ready for implementation.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FhzC1nSK1i7Pis1wjPNoYq', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "29c08f87", "message": "Created project: Timeline Focus Preservation Fix", "summary": {"project_id": "29c08f87", "project_name": "Timeline Focus Preservation Fix", "description": "Implement timeline scroll preservation during data refresh to prevent user focus disruption in HorizontalTimelineView component. Milestone 1 analysis complete, ready for implementation.", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-17T01:04:30.032097", "updated_at": "2026-01-17T01:04:30.032097", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-17T01:04:30.032097", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Timeline Focus Preservation Fix\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SNxbGCTYYoCEpQKiGDgqdC', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': "# Timeline Focus Preservation Fix - Requirements Document\n\n## Project Vision\nFix the HorizontalTimelineView component to preserve user scroll position and view focus during data refresh operations. The current implementation causes disruptive view resets that interrupt user workflow and degrade user experience.\n\n## Core Objectives\n1. **View Stability**: Maintain user's scroll position during data refresh operations\n2. **Performance Optimization**: Prevent unnecessary component re-renders during updates\n3. **User Experience**: Eliminate view disruption and unexpected navigation jumps\n4. **Backward Compatibility**: Preserve all existing HorizontalTimelineView functionality\n5. **Code Quality**: Implement solution following TDD methodology and React best practices\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Core Fix Components\n- **Scroll Position Management**: Track and preserve horizontal/vertical scroll positions\n- **Selective Re-rendering**: Update only data that has changed, not view state\n- **State Isolation**: Separate data refresh logic from view state management\n- **Memory Management**: Efficient handling of view state without memory leaks\n- **Performance Monitoring**: Track render performance and view stability metrics\n\n### User Experience Requirements\n- **Seamless Updates**: Data refresh occurs without visible interruption to user\n- **Position Preservation**: Exact scroll position maintained across refresh cycles\n- **Smooth Performance**: No lag or stuttering during refresh operations\n- **Visual Consistency**: No unexpected view shifts or layout jumps\n- **Responsive Behavior**: Works consistently across different screen sizes\n\n### Technical Implementation\n- **Custom Hooks**: useViewState and useDataRefresh for modular functionality\n- **Component Wrapper**: TimelineContainer to integrate scroll preservation\n- **Memoized Rendering**: Selective updates using React.memo and useMemo\n- **Event Management**: Proper scroll event handling and cleanup\n- **Cross-browser Support**: Consistent behavior across modern browsers\n\n## Technical Requirements\n\n### Frontend (React)\n- **Custom Hook Architecture**: \n  - `useViewState` for scroll position tracking and restoration\n  - `useDataRefresh` for controlled data updates without view disruption\n- **Component Structure**:\n  - `TimelineContainer` wrapper around existing HorizontalTimelineView\n  - `MemoizedTimelineItems` for selective rendering optimization\n- **Performance Optimization**: React.memo, useMemo, and useCallback for efficient updates\n- **State Management**: Minimal state changes to prevent unnecessary re-renders\n\n### Integration Requirements\n- **Existing Component Preservation**: HorizontalTimelineView core functionality unchanged\n- **API Compatibility**: Maintain current data fetching and refresh mechanisms\n- **Event Handling**: Proper integration with existing scroll and interaction events\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful fallback if scroll preservation fails\n\n### Implementation Tasks (from frontend_tasks_m1.md)\n1. **Custom Hooks Creation** (2-4 hours)\n   - useViewState for scroll position management\n   - useDataRefresh for controlled data updates\n\n2. **Memoized Components** (4-6 hours)\n   - React.memo optimization for timeline items\n   - Stable key generation for efficient diffing\n\n3. **Container Integration** (5-7 hours)\n   - TimelineContainer wrapper implementation\n   - Integration of view state preservation logic\n\n4. **Performance Monitoring** (2-4 hours)\n   - Analytics for view stability events\n   - Render time tracking and optimization metrics\n\n5. **Cross-Browser Testing** (4-6 hours)\n   - Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge compatibility\n   - Mobile and desktop responsive behavior\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n### Performance\n- Scroll preservation overhead: < 5ms per refresh\n- Memory usage: No significant increase during extended use\n- Render performance: Maintain 60 FPS during scroll operations\n- Data refresh speed: No impact on current refresh performance\n\n### Accessibility\n- Keyboard navigation: Preserve focus state during refresh\n- Screen reader compatibility: No accessibility regressions\n- High contrast mode: Maintain visual consistency\n- Reduced motion: Respect user motion preferences\n\n### Browser Support\n- Modern browsers: Chrome 90+, Firefox 88+, Safari 14+, Edge 90+\n- Scroll behavior: Consistent across different scrolling mechanisms\n- Performance: Optimized for both desktop and mobile devices\n\n### Reliability\n- Fallback mechanism: Graceful degradation if scroll preservation fails\n- Error recovery: No application crashes due to view state issues\n- Memory management: Proper cleanup of scroll event listeners\n- Edge cases: Handle rapid refresh cycles and extreme scroll positions\n\n## Success Criteria\n1. **User Focus Preservation**: Users maintain their viewing position during data refresh (100% success rate)\n2. **Performance Metrics**: No measurable performance degradation in scroll or render operations\n3. **Cross-Browser Compatibility**: Consistent behavior across all supported browsers\n4. **Test Coverage**: 90% unit test coverage, 100% integration test coverage for view management\n5. **User Experience**: No user-reported view disruption issues after implementation\n\n## Technical Constraints\n- **Performance Budget**: Maximum 5ms overhead per refresh operation\n- **Memory Limit**: No more than 2MB additional memory usage\n- **Bundle Size**: Implementation should not increase bundle size by more than 10KB\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Zero breaking changes to existing HorizontalTimelineView API\n\n## Implementation Strategy (TDD Approach)\n1. **Test First**: Write comprehensive tests for scroll position management\n2. **Red-Green-Refactor**: Implement minimal code to pass tests, then optimize\n3. **Integration Testing**: Test complete user interaction flows\n4. **Performance Testing**: Benchmark before and after implementation\n5. **Cross-browser Validation**: Ensure consistent behavior across target browsers\n\n## Dependencies\n- **React**: Current version (18+) with hooks support\n- **Existing Components**: HorizontalTimelineView component structure\n- **Testing Framework**: Jest and React Testing Library setup\n- **Development Environment**: Access to target browsers for testing\n\n## Assumptions Made\n- **Component Structure**: HorizontalTimelineView uses standard React patterns\n- **Data Refresh Pattern**: Current data refresh triggers via useEffect/props changes\n- **Scroll Implementation**: Standard browser scroll APIs are available\n- **Performance Requirements**: Current performance is acceptable baseline\n- **Browser Support**: Target modern browsers with CSS custom properties\n\n## Out of Scope\n- **Complete Component Redesign**: Major architectural changes to timeline view\n- **Advanced Animation**: Complex transition effects during updates\n- **Mobile Native**: React Native or mobile app specific optimizations\n- **Real-time Features**: WebSocket or real-time data streaming optimizations\n- **Accessibility Overhaul**: Major accessibility improvements beyond maintaining current level\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- **Feature Flags**: Implementation behind feature flag for safe rollback\n- **Progressive Enhancement**: Core functionality works even if scroll preservation fails\n- **Monitoring**: Performance and error tracking for production issues\n- **Rollback Plan**: Quick revert process if issues arise in production\n\n## Deliverables\n1. **Custom Hooks**: useViewState and useDataRefresh implementations\n2. **Container Component**: TimelineContainer wrapper with scroll preservation\n3. **Memoized Components**: Optimized timeline item rendering\n4. **Test Suite**: Comprehensive unit and integration tests\n5. **Performance Documentation**: Before/after performance analysis\n6. **Implementation Guide**: Documentation for future maintenance and extension"}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SNxbGCTYYoCEpQKiGDgqdC', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260117_010506.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260117_010506.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TogTH1miniVL4HnnGZTf3y', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '29c08f87', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements analysis complete. Found comprehensive documentation for timeline focus preservation fix. Milestone 1 (investigation & architecture) already completed with detailed implementation plan. Ready to proceed with development phase.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TogTH1miniVL4HnnGZTf3y', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Ew2fuBcAHXHVqJCtgRXKiq', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '29c08f87', 'description': 'Implement timeline focus preservation fix with TDD methodology. 