{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 12:57:38", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-35b12ff6-dd56-451d-8fb0-c3a373f3a788', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Backend Lead Model Optimization"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Csq9yACAXhCFc5ytDrNH8i', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Csq9yACAXhCFc5ytDrNH8i', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# TDD Coordinator Model Update - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nUpdate the TDD Coordinator agent\'s model configuration to use the \'sonnet\' model for cost optimization, while maintaining functionality and performance.\\n\\n## Background\\nThe TDD Coordinator agent currently has a 95.24% success rate, indicating consistent high performance. This presents an opportunity to optimize costs by switching to a more cost-effective model without compromising functionality.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Update TDD Coordinator\'s model configuration from current model to \'sonnet\'\\n2. Verify syntax correctness of the configuration change\\n3. Update any related configuration files if needed\\n4. Ensure no functionality is lost in the transition\\n\\n## Scope\\n### In Scope\\n- Locate TDD Coordinator agent definition file\\n- Update ## Model Preference section to use \'sonnet\' model\\n- Validate configuration syntax\\n- Review and update any related configuration dependencies\\n- Document changes made\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Performance testing of the new model (agent already has high success rate)\\n- Changing other agents\' model configurations\\n- Cost analysis calculations\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. TDD Coordinator agent definition file successfully updated with \'sonnet\' model\\n2. Configuration syntax is valid\\n3. No breaking changes introduced\\n4. All related configurations updated appropriately\\n5. Changes documented and verified\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Must maintain current agent functionality\\n- Must follow existing configuration file format\\n- Changes must be backward compatible\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- TDD Coordinator agent definition exists in standard location\\n- \'sonnet\' model is available and supported\\n- Current high success rate indicates model change will not impact performance significantly\\n- Standard markdown-based agent definition format is used\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. Updated TDD Coordinator agent definition file\\n2. Verification of syntax correctness\\n3. Documentation of changes made\\n4. Status report confirming successful update"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SWMq2KD9mNmJ4ojLadMNTG', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Backend Lead Model Optimization', 'description': "Update TDD Coordinator agent's model configuration to use 'sonnet' model for cost optimization"}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SWMq2KD9mNmJ4ojLadMNTG', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "68054274", "message": "Created project: Backend Lead Model Optimization", "summary": {"project_id": "68054274", "project_name": "Backend Lead Model Optimization", "description": "Update TDD Coordinator agent\'s model configuration to use \'sonnet\' model for cost optimization", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-17T12:57:11.918821", "updated_at": "2026-01-17T12:57:11.918821", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-17T12:57:11.918821", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Backend Lead Model Optimization\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01APzMYsjL737w6PWnKfhpMb', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01APzMYsjL737w6PWnKfhpMb', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MfChfxzihx5nF2HzbxHogL', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MfChfxzihx5nF2HzbxHogL', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Created architectural proposal for Frontend Coordinator model preference update with a minimal, low-risk approach", "key_decisions": ["Use targeted configuration update approach", "Maintain existing file structure", "Preserve all existing agent configurations", "Validate syntax and structure before deployment"], "self_analysis": "The architecture proposal successfully addresses the requirements with a minimalist, low-risk strategy. The approach focuses on precise, constrained changes while maintaining system integrity and performance characteristics. The documentation provides clear guidance for implementation and highlights potential considerations."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention 