/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/coordinators/frontend_coordinator.md`\\n   - Responsibility: Define agent model preference and capabilities\\n   - Change: Update model from \'haiku\' to \'sonnet\'\\n\\n2. **Configuration Loader**\\n   - Existing system that reads markdown configuration\\n   - Must support \'sonnet\' model identifier\\n   - No modifications required to loader itself\\n\\n## D) File/Directory Structure\\n```\\nensemble/\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 coordinators/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 frontend_coordinator.md  # Target file for update\\n```\\n\\n## E) Data Model\\n- **Model Preference**: Simple string value\\n- **Current State**: `haiku`\\n- **Target State**: `sonnet`\\n\\n## F) Update Strategy\\n1. Direct text replacement in markdown file\\n2. Preserve all existing formatting\\n3. Validate file syntax post-update\\n\\n## G) Deployment Strategy\\n- Manual update of configuration file\\n- No runtime or system-level deployments required\\n- Version control commit with descriptive message\\n\\n## H) Testing Strategy\\n1. **Syntax Validation**\\n   - Verify markdown structure remains intact\\n   - Confirm no unintended formatting changes\\n\\n2. **Configuration Validation**\\n   - Verify \'sonnet\' model can be correctly read\\n   - Confirm no changes to other configuration sections\\n\\n## I) Alternatives Considered\\n1. Complete agent redefinition (Rejected: Unnecessarily complex)\\n2. Phased model transition (Rejected: Introduces complexity)\\n3. Direct text replacement (Chosen: Minimal risk, direct approach)\\n\\n## J) Risks and Mitigations\\n- **Risk**: Model compatibility issues\\n  - **Mitigation**: Verify \'sonnet\' model\'s compatibility beforehand\\n- **Risk**: Unintended configuration changes\\n  - **Mitigation**: Strict syntax validation, manual review\\n\\n## K) Open Questions\\n- Confirm \'sonnet\' model\'s pricing and performance characteristics\\n- Validate cost savings expectation\\n\\n## Performance Impact Analysis\\n- Current Success Rate: 98.41%\\n- Expected Change: Minimal to no performance deviation\\n- Primary Goal: Cost optimization\\n\\n## Recommendation\\nProceed with the proposed update, replacing \'haiku\' with \'sonnet\' in the Frontend Coordinator\'s configuration file."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EqReUAgLWwmkmEMeTKJCtD', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EqReUAgLWwmkmEMeTKJCtD', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Frontend Coordinator Model Update - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nUpdate the Frontend Coordinator agent definition to use the \'sonnet\' model instead of the current \'haiku\' model for cost optimization, while maintaining the agent\'s excellent performance (98.41% success rate).\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Primary**: Change model preference from \'haiku\' to \'sonnet\' in Frontend Coordinator definition\\n2. **Verification**: Ensure syntax correctness and proper configuration\\n3. **Validation**: Confirm no breaking changes to agent functionality\\n4. **Documentation**: Record the change and rationale\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Modify the \\"## Model Preference\\" section in `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/coordinators/frontend_coordinator.md`\\n- Update model preference from \\"haiku\\" to \\"sonnet\\"\\n- Verify file syntax and structure integrity\\n- Validate related configuration consistency\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Changes to other agent definitions\\n- Modifications to agent behavior or capabilities\\n- Updates to runtime system or configuration loading\\n- Testing the model change in live environment\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n- **FR-1**: Model preference must be changed from \\"haiku\\" to \\"sonnet\\"\\n- **FR-2**: All other sections of the agent definition must remain unchanged\\n- **FR-3**: File must maintain valid markdown structure\\n- **FR-4**: Agent capabilities and permissions must remain identical\\n\\n### Non-Functional Requirements\\n- **NFR-1**: Change must be backward compatible with current configuration system\\n- **NFR-2**: No impact on agent\'s existing success rate or performance characteristics\\n- **NFR-3**: Change must be easily reversible if needed\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- \\u2705 Frontend Coordinator definition file updated with \\"sonnet\\" model preference\\n- \\u2705 File syntax validation passes\\n- \\u2705 All other configuration sections preserved exactly\\n- \\u2705 Change committed to version control with descriptive message\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Must preserve exact formatting and structure of existing file\\n- Cannot modify agent permissions, tools, or capabilities\\n- Must maintain consistency with other model preference formats in the system\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- The \'sonnet\' model is available and compatible with the Frontend Coordinator\'s role\\n- The configuration loading system supports the \'sonnet\' model identifier\\n- Cost optimization is the primary driver for this change\\n- No behavioral changes are expected from the model switch\\n\\n## Technical Details\\n- **Target File**: `/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/coordinators/frontend_coordinator.md`\\n- **Section to Update**: `## Model Preference`\\n- **Current Value**: `haiku`\\n- **New Value**: `sonnet`\\n- **Configuration Format**: Simple text value under the Model Preference heading\\n\\n## Rationale\\nThe Frontend Coordinator has demonstrated exceptional performance with a 98.41% success rate, indicating that it can maintain effectiveness with a more cost-efficient model. The \'sonnet\' model provides a balance of capability and cost that aligns with optimization goals while preserving the agent\'s proven effectiveness."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ADjAQGudLHRREbGRKLLUyy', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Frontend Coordinator Model Update Testing', 'description': 'Comprehensive test strategy for updating Frontend Coordinator from haiku to sonnet model'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01ADjAQGudLHRREbGRKLLUyy', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "64be91ba", "message": "Created project: Frontend Coordinator Model Update Testing", "summary": {"project_id": "64be91ba", "project_name": "Frontend Coordinator Model Update Testing", "description": "Comprehensive test strategy for updating Frontend Coordinator from haiku to sonnet model", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-17T12:57:50.935158", "updated_at": "2026-01-17T12:57:50.935158", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-17T12:57:50.935158", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Frontend Coordinator Model Update Testing\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.9\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'n